# Frequency comparison across units

Verifies mixed-unit comparisons scale the coarser frequency to the finer unit. One kilohertz equals one thousand hertz, and one megahertz equals one thousand kilohertz across all equality boundaries.

>>> source
kilo: int = 1khz
thousand: int = 1000hz
print(kilo == thousand)
print(kilo != thousand)
print(kilo <= thousand)
print(kilo >= thousand)
mega: int = 1mhz
print(mega > 1000khz)
print(mega == 1000khz)

<<< stdout
true
false
true
true
false
true

<<< stderr
